{
  "$schema": "../../schema/livery.schema.json",
  "id": "dunkin",
  "airline": "JBU",
  "name": "Dunkin' (Brewing Altitude)",
  "kind": "special",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "A320",
  "from": "2025-05",
  "description": "Fuselage: Dunkin' orange crown and belly with a broad raspberry-pink wave sweeping through the middle from the pink nose: its upper edge crests above the forward windows and again over the wing and dips to the window line between and aft of the wing, its lower edge rises from the chin to the forward door's foot, falls low behind the wing and rises again aft; behind the aft door the pink takes the whole tail cone, with orange round the stabilizer's root. Titles: 'jetBlue', a white airplane seen from above, then 'DUNKIN'' in white along the forward windows. Tail: a tilted Dunkin' coffee cup: a pink cup outlined in thick white with a big white 'D', its white lid band across the fin and a white sip hole in the pink lid above; orange outside the cup at the fin's root and along the trailing edge. The cup's rounded white outline runs from the fin down onto the rear fuselage as one shape, its foot at the belly under the stabilizer. Engines and wingtip fences orange.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250512190550/en/JetBlue-Runs-on-Dunkin-With-New-Special-Livery",
